## Goal
LANDMARKS for chapter-4 combat rooms (inside a giant clock tower). The game places 1-3 of these big set pieces per room near corners or inside the room so the room is not a plain rectangle; players walk around them and they block bullets. They are seen from a top-down camera ~55 deg, so the TOP and the silhouette must read; they are BIG solid blockers, not see-through scaffolds (gaps smaller than ~0.5 m are fine, but the footprint must be mostly filled at the base so nothing walks through).
Each piece: ONE joined mesh named exactly as listed, origin at the BOTTOM CENTRE, +Y front, exported to `Game/Assets/Art/Characters/Ch4/Kit_<Name>.fbx`. 6-8 role materials each, rich carving (rivets, gear-tooth rims, relief dials, stacked moldings, inset panels), up to ~8000 triangles each.

## Pieces (footprint W (X) x D (Y) x H (Z), metres)
1. `LM_Clockwork` (5.0 x 4.0 x 3.2) - a fallen chunk of clock movement: a big `brass` gear (diameter 3.2) lying tilted ~20 deg on a riveted `iron_dark` base block (5.0 x 4.0 x 0.8), a second smaller `steel` gear meshing with it, an escapement anchor (`silver`) and a coiled mainspring drum (`brass_dark` with `steel` spring coils) on the other side, `red_lacquer` bolt caps.
2. `LM_PendulumCase` (3.6 x 2.6 x 4.6) - a tall grandfather-clock-like cabinet standing in the room: `wood_dark` case with carved `wood` panels and `gold` trim, a `dial_face` clock face with `dial_mark` raised Roman-numeral bars and `steel` hands at the top, a `glass` window in the long body showing a `brass` pendulum disc and `steel` rod, a stepped `stone_dark` plinth (3.6 x 2.6 x 0.5), a broken top pediment with a cracked `gold` finial; `velvet` inside the window back.
3. `LM_GearStack` (4.4 x 4.4 x 2.6) - a stack of three horizontal gear discs of decreasing size (`brass`, `steel`, `brass_dark`), each with spokes and teeth, on a shared `iron` axle with `silver` hub caps; a `iron_dark` octagonal floor mount with rivets; a few loose `copper` cogs leaning at the base.
4. `LM_BellFrame` (4.2 x 3.0 x 4.0) - a sturdy bell-tower frame: two `wood_dark` A-frame posts braced with `iron` straps and rivets, a heavy crossbeam with `brass` caps, a large `copper` bell (mouth diameter 2.0) hanging low so its lip is ~0.5 above the floor with a `brass` lip ring, `dial_mark` tick band and `iron_dark` clapper, a `stone` footing slab under everything; `ribbon_red` rope tied to the clapper.
5. `LM_DialFragment` (5.2 x 2.4 x 3.4) - a broken piece of the giant outer clock face stuck upright into the floor: a thick curved slab (arc of a 10 m circle, 0.6 thick) of `dial_face` with big `dial_mark` raised Roman-numeral bars and a `gold` outer rim molding, the broken edge showing `stone_dark` core and `iron` rebar stubs; a huge `steel` minute-hand fragment leaning against it; a rubble mound of `stone` chunks at the base; a few `starlight` bits glinting in the cracks.

Print `EXPORTED <Name> <tris> <dims>` per piece and `DONE`.
Preview: all pieces in a row at their real sizes, 1800x1000, Workbench flat MATERIAL colours (distinct viewport colour per material name), camera ~55 deg from above-front, to `Art/tools/specs/blender_kit_ch4_landmarks_preview.png`.
